spacemit-firmware (1.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Ship a unified flashing script (flash-firmware.sh) that writes the
    whole boot-chain firmware set provided by the dependency packages
    (bootinfo, FSBL and the U-Boot environment from u-boot-spl-spacemit,
    OpenSBI, ESOS, and EDK2 when booted via UEFI) in one transaction:
    every image is preflight-checked, NOR regions are erased before
    being written and every image is read back and verified.
  * Take over the flashing that used to live in the postinsts of
    edk2-spacemit, opensbi-spacemit, esos-spacemit and
    u-boot-spl-spacemit; those packages now only ship their images.
  * Add dpkg triggers on the firmware image directories so that
    upgrading any of those packages reflashes the affected images even
    when this metapackage's own version does not change.
  * d/control: depend on kmod and mtd-utils for modprobe, flashcp and
    mtd_debug, which the flashing script uses directly.

 -- Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:45:49 +0200

spacemit-firmware (1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: metapackage pulling in the SpacemiT firmware/boot
    packages (EDK2, EC firmware, OpenSBI, U-Boot SPL, ESOS).

